From: Marco Martins
Subject: mac80211: 512 queue flows instead of 4096

For a 16 MB access point with a handful of clients: the flow table and its
CoDel state take 64 bytes per flow, 256 KB at 4096 flows and 32 KB at 512.
Fewer flows only means unrelated traffic shares a queue more often.
---
--- a/net/mac80211/tx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/tx.c
@@ -1581,7 +1581,7 @@
 	bool supp_vht = false;
 	enum nl80211_band band;
 
-	ret = fq_init(fq, 4096);
+	ret = fq_init(fq, 512);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
